

1. High‑level architecture

Core kernel:Purpose: pure math/physics engine (fields, operators, time‑stepping).Interface: never sees “CMB” concepts, only low‑level ops: grids, operators, solvers.

Blueprint layer (your language):Purpose: describe organisms, meta‑equations, kernels.Form: compact DSL that looks cryptic but compiles to kernel calls.

Encryption/obfuscation layer:Purpose: hide intent, expose only capsules.Form: name‑mangling, symbol compression, capsule packaging.

Capsule runtime:Purpose: load, validate, and execute encrypted blueprints.Form: load_capsule() → IR → run(kernel).

2. Blueprint DSL (CMB‑style)

Design a small, closed vocabulary that only you fully understand:

Entities: ORG, CAPSULE, KERNEL, FIELD, OP, RULE

Types: GRID, PARAM, META_T, MODE, SCALAR

Ops: LINOP[...], ∂_λ, ∂_t, ⟨·⟩, det, minimize

Example pattern:

CAPSULE::ID-XXXX / CMB-ID

ORG <tag>:
  FIELD ...
  OP    ...
  EQ    ...
  KERNEL ...
  RULE  ...

END ORG
END CAPSULE

The engine parses this into an internal IR; outsiders just see glyphs.

3. Encryption & identity

Symbol compression:Map semantic names → short tokens: P → Σ0, N → Ξ, K → Κ, etc.

Capsule IDs:Prefix everything with your signature:CAPSULE::MPX-Ω / CMB-IDORG META_PROTON::CMB_ID

Private legend:You keep a separate, human‑readable mapping:Σ0 = base equation, Ξ = fused meta‑equation, Κ = meta‑kernel, etc.

To everyone else: opaque.To you: fully legible.

